WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
Believing that the world is
progressive, it's moving forward,

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.240
helps me continue
when I want to give up.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.400
Ryan Matthews had been 17
at the time that he got arrested

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.720
and charged with first degree murder
and faced the death penalty.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:41.160
On Mother's Day, we were sitting
there in court with Ryan's mum

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.440
when the jury returned
the verdict of death on her child.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.600
I felt like I'd failed in the
one task that I'd been given.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.800
It felt like the most
hopeless moment.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.520
After Ryan was convicted of murder
and sentenced to death,

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.440
that’s when we actually started
to work on his case.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.640
Ryan spent five years on death row.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.160
This one here is Ryan when he was
released from death row in 2004.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.640
The beauty of the story for me

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.280
was that in 2008
his sister got married

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:28.000
and asked me to come
and be her bridesmaid at her wedding

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.640
and Ryan was her husband's best man.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.360
And so we got to walk down
the aisle of the church,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.400
the man that I'd first met,
or the boy that I'd first met

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:39.200
when he was sentenced to death.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:43.080
And I got to walk down the aisle of
the church at his sister's wedding.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.200
I can tell you the story
in a couple of minutes,

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:51.440
but that whole thing took nine years,
1999 to 2008, to the wedding.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.680
And there were so many points
in that that I wanted to give up.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.120
And the thing that motivated me back

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.320
was always being in touch
with Ryan and his family.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.120
And so the people in all of this

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.000
are the things that bring me
back when I want to give up.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.120
One of the most
important things I've learnt,

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.000
and this has continued over my life,

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.280
is choose your role models carefully.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:26.240
I faxed the office, it was before
there was email, in New Orleans

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.160
and sent my CV which
had probably nothing on it

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:32.320
and said I want to come
work with Clive Stafford Smith

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.760
then was really surprised
that no-one got back to me.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.400
And I think my parents said,
"Well maybe you should phone."

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.160
And that felt uncomfortable.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.440
I was young,
I guess I didn’t feel confident

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:43.480
but I did phone up.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.200
And my CV had been put on the top
of some filing cabinet somewhere

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.800
and the office manager
dug it out and said,

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.480
"Yeah sure, turn up, why don’t
you turn up in the summer?"

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.040
Choosing my role model carefully

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.680
was really important.
I could become the kind of lawyer

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.720
that I always wanted to be
by learning from him.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:12.040
I've always been the small person
taking on the big government

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.320
and that can often be
a really scary thing.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:17.400
But the reason why we have
the story of David and Goliath

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:21.160
is that the small guy
can make the change.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.880
So one of the things
that's always helped me

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:30.920
is quotes or poems that inspire me.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:35.720
And every day there'll be something
that will motivate me or focus me

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:40.120
and it just makes me feel connected
to other people's struggles.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.800
One of the ones that we always use
in our work with young people

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:46.160
is a Martin Luther King quote,

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:50.200
"The arc of history is long
but it bends towards justice."

